  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {現実|げんじつ}に{即|そく}する (conform to reality)\n- {時代|じだい}に{即|そく}する (suit the times)\n- {法律|ほうりつ}に{即|そく}する (be in accordance with the law)\n- {実態|じったい}に{即|そく}する (be based on the actual situation)\n\nUSAGE:\nA formal verb most commonly seen in the た-form as {即|そく}した (modifying a noun) or the て-form {即|そく}して (as an adverbial phrase). The pattern ～に{即|そく}した means \"suited to ~\" or \"based on ~.\" Rarely used in casual speech — {合|あ}う or {合|あ}わせる are more everyday alternatives.",
